    "created_at": "2022-05-19T21:11:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-19T21:11:45Z",
    "body": "IMO websites should never be able to access the browser chrome in any way. If a website moved my focus to browser UI automatically, I would be very confused. Additionally, this means that to do anything useful, the website would need to assume details about how the browser chrome is layed out - which will break not just between different browsers, but also with updates.\r\n\r\nSimilarly for iframes, it seems like a security risk to allow a child iframe to move the focus of the parent, or a parent iframe to move the focus inside a cross-origin iframe. A website should already be able to access the dom of a same-origin iframe normally anyways.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
